[Music]  hey folks you probably got a good look  at diablo 4 during the xbox showcase  however we have a little bit of extra  footage that we wanted to show off uh  just to give you guys a better  understanding of the gameplay  specifically we have footage of the  necromancer one of the classes they just  announced as well as some pvp stuff and  a world boss uh joining me is eric tay  he is the blizzard uh diablo expert uh  so we had to get him on here to kind of  go over some of the cool stuff that he  noticed yeah thanks for having me jake  and uh hello to all the fans but it's  really exciting to see more diablo 4 of  course uh seeing the necromancer get  revealed not my personal favorite class  of of you know the diablo  timeline but you know i know there's a  lot of folks that enjoy the class and  we're getting to see kind of just some  tried and true right some corpse explode  and and kind of going through a dungeon  with just a golem which is interesting  because you know the necro is known so  much for being a sumner class and we're  gonna you know see some variations of of  the necromancer gameplay throughout this  kind of first clip um we'll kind of let  this play through a little bit and then  i can get into some of the other  stuff in a little bit  now we're out in the kind of like open  world um here different class kind of  build here you have skeletal warriors  you have skeletal mages um what looks  like maybe teeth from kind of diablo 2  or variation of bone spear  as well as some cursing going on we  don't get context in terms of like what  exactly each of those skills are the  only thing that i saw through these  clips that we got are just more about  the different variations for the the  summoning which is you know the primary  core of a necromancer um but you know i  can kind of break some of those down so  the skeletal warriors that are kind of  out there right now  are probably um either skirmishers or  reapers uh there's three there's three  variations skirmishers defenders and  reapers the defender which is the only  tool tip that we got through this kind  of gameplay is  geared towards uh having durable shield  bearers with 15 more life you'll see  some defender  uh  skeletal wars later in the later part of  this clip but um you know you can  upgrade it uh one of two ways one of the  ways you know every 10 seconds your  skeletal defenders will negate the next  instance of direct damage they would  take  if you decide to want to sacrifice it  which is one of the three options you'll  gain 15  um non-physical resistance but you'll no  longer be able to raise skeletons the  skeletal mages there's three options  there's shadow cold and bone  for example with cold as one of the  upgrades each time your cold mages  damage enemies with their primary attack  you gain two essence if you want to  sacrifice the uh cold skeletal mage  you'll deal 15  increased damage to vulnerable enemies  but again no longer able to summon  skeletal mages um and then with the the  golems there's bone blood or iron uh in  this clip you're seeing iron so i'll  just like break down what iron does iron  golem will slam the ground and stun  enemies and every fifth iron golem  attack causes a shock wave dealing x  percent damage to primary enemy and  enemy behind it that's that's one of the  two upgrades for the iron golem and then  if you decide to sacrifice the iron  golem uh you'll deal 30  increased critical strike damage um but  you can't summon a golem anymore  i've never enjoyed the summoning aspect  of necromancers even though that that's  kind of what the class does so it's kind  of cool to have this passive ability of  trading off your summons to make your  necromancer stronger essentially um but  what we're seeing in this clip is you  have the defender skeletal  warriors that i mentioned as well as  iron golem there's legendaries that  they're not picking up  presumably to you know keep some of that  hidden uh although i know a lot of folks  probably want to see what those are  and then you have either a bone spear  kind of like variant where it is  hitting the wall and then bouncing back  and kind of making three bone shards or  like smaller bone shards um  don't know if that's an upgrade for for  like bone sphere or teeth i'm not sure  which one it is that looks more like  bone spear though um or if it's kind of  like a legendary effect that's like on  one of the necromancers items right now  on on this specific character one thing  to just note a lot of that information  uh you gathered from a build that's not  finals like some of that could change so  don't take everything as gospel that  we're saying but anyway back to the  gameplay  man  [Applause]  yes  we're getting some pvp here which is  something uh they're kind of bringing  back right it was pretty big in d2 but  uh was absent in d3 yeah like it's it's  cool to see it come back uh you know  there's definitely a lot of folks that  enjoy pvp um so don't know how it'll  interact with you know what end game or  like mid game looks like or what kind of  rewards you even get from it but you  know it does give that extra flavor of  kind of builds and  gear that you might want to use  specifically for pvp that might not be  necessarily good for pve but you know is  catered to just  fighting other players  huh  all right so the last clip we got is a  world boss um and this boss looks pretty  impressive but you were noticing some  similarities to other  d3 bosses right yeah just a little bit  you'll you'll see later on like in the  clip when it kind of does some summons  where like it's summoned some treasure  goblins kind of eerily similar to greed  from diablo 3 where you know you take  your puzzle ring and and put that in the  cube so that you could get this kind of  like secret level um but yeah it's a  pretty big spectacle you know having a  big boss out in the field with um i  tried to count them there's definitely  at least seven um  characters but i think you can have up  to eight as i mentioned previously  there's the kind of the goblins running  off it saddens me that they don't try to  chase them to kind of kill them to get  the gear that presumably they would drop  but you know hey we're focusing on dps  on the the world boss here and i think  the other one cool thing that i i  noticed is it kind of feels a little bit  like monster huntery where  um you know at the start of the fight  the boss isn't as beat up it doesn't  have as many scars but kind of like over  time you kind of see a little bit more  like  cuts and and a little bit more bleeding  from the from the boss  but um yeah just just cool to have a an  open area where you can kind of team up  with other players and and kind of  tackle a big boss you know and get some  hopefully good gear  and that's it on the diablo 4 gameplay  thank you all for watching and if you  want to check out more diablo coverage  we have a couple videos on gamespot  right now including an interview with  some of the developers that i highly  recommend you check out see you next  time

